I came to draw my wa[F7sus4]ter when nobody was a[Bb]round
A tired Jewish s[Gm7]tranger sitting quiet by the [Eb]stone
Said give me a drink, and I [F7sus4]said why ask me, you should leave me a[Cm7]lone
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
If you knew the gift of [Dm7]God and who it is who speaks to [Eb]you
